From: Craterbrain <58347640+Craterbrain@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:51:34 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 16/78] PlaitOS: navigation bar long-press actions (home, back)
 with power menu and kill app

Selective port of LineageOS's hardware keys custom rebinding (frameworks_base 61456c0d9311,
Phil Tunstall et al.): the performKeyAction dispatcher and SystemUI's hand-off of a home
long press to PhoneWindowManager, plus DeviceKeysConstants.Action and ActionUtils
(killForegroundApp, switchToLastApp) from lineage-sdk (The LineageOS Project, Apache-2.0).

PlaitOS changes: only the 3-button navigation bar keys (home long press, back long press);
a new POWER_MENU action; Settings.System plait_home_long_press_action and
plait_back_long_press_action, where unset keeps the stock behavior (assistant on home);
screenshots through ScreenshotHelper as Android 17 does; framework string for the kill toast.

Co-authored-by: Phil Tunstall <ptunstall@gmail.com>
